176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) is a field of computer science concerned with developing systems that can perform tasks that normally require human-like intelligence, such as learning from data, recognising patterns, making predictions and supporting decisions. Machine Learning \(ML\) is a major part of AI in which computer systems learn useful patterns from data rather than relying only on explicitly written rules.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (During the internship, the focus was on understanding AI/ML from a practical perspective. The learning process connected fundamental concepts with implementation-oriented activities, helping build an understanding of how AI solutions are developed, tested, evaluated and documented.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
